#import "/modern-iaf/manuals/layout/manual.typ": *

#idx("Four-ship")#idx("Formation")#idx("Wingmen")The fourth #term("lesson") of the Sufa: mission 2014, from Ramon, runway 25R. You lead Kidon 1, a four-ship of Sufas. You are Kidon 1-1; Kidon 1-2, 1-3 and 1-4 are flown by the computer. Kidon 1-3 leads the second pair.

=== Where the flight starts <lesson-four-ship-start>

The four jets stand cold in Ramon's four Sufa shelters: you in S2, Kidon 1-2 in S3, Kidon 1-3 in S1 and Kidon 1-4 in S5. The wingmen carry the same #term("loadout") as your jet. The briefing's map shows the taxi route and the route of the flight.

=== The flight's start-up and taxi <lesson-four-ship-taxi>

#idx("Four-ship, start-up")Call the #term("tower") and request start-up, as in the Take-off lesson (@lesson-takeoff). The tower's #term("clearance") is the whole flight's: Kidon 1-2 starts its engine 3 seconds after the clearance, Kidon 1-3 3 seconds later, Kidon 1-4 3 seconds after that. If you start your engine without the call, the wingmen start with you.

Each wingman waits in its shelter until the jet ahead of it has moved 150 m: Kidon 1-2 behind you, Kidon 1-3 behind Kidon 1-2, Kidon 1-4 behind Kidon 1-3. Each taxis behind the one ahead on its shelter's taxi route and keeps its distance.

=== The take-off and the join-up <lesson-four-ship-takeoff>

#idx("Four-ship, take-off")The wingmen take off in a stream: each starts its roll when the jet ahead passes 50 knots on the runway. Once in the air, each flies to its place in the fingertip formation on you and keeps it, also in your turns: Kidon 1-2 60 m behind on your left, Kidon 1-3 60 m behind on your right, Kidon 1-4 60 m behind Kidon 1-3 on its right.

A wingman that comes too near another jet pulls away from it, then flies back to its place.

=== The pairs and threats <lesson-four-ship-pairs>

#idx("Four-ship, pairs")The flight flies as two pairs: Kidon 1-2 with you, Kidon 1-4 with Kidon 1-3. When Kidon 1-3 leaves the formation, Kidon 1-4 goes with it.

#idx("Four-ship, threats")A wingman locked by a radar, or with a missile fired at it, turns hard against it about a second later: it puts a radar off its wing and turns into a heat-seeking missile. It turns its jammer on. Against a missile it drops chaff, or flares against a heat-seeking one: once at the launch and again in the missile's last seconds. Against a lock alone it only turns and jams. Five seconds after the threat is gone, it flies back to its place.

=== The way home <lesson-four-ship-home>

#idx("Four-ship, landing")When you lower the gear within 20 km of Ramon, or fly low with the gear down, the wingmen go home one after the other: Kidon 1-2 first, Kidon 1-3 20 seconds later, then Kidon 1-4. Each flies the circuit, lands, taxis to its own shelter and stops its engine. A wingman low on fuel goes home on its own.

#idx("Four-ship, landing calls")The tower talks to each wingman on the way in. As it turns onto its final approach: "Kidon 1-2, cleared to land runway 25 right"; once its landing roll has stopped: "Kidon 1-2, welcome back, taxi to parking". The wingman answers with its callsign. Your own landing call is on the tower's menu (@tower-landing).

On the taxiways a wingman slows before each turn and stops behind any jet of the flight in its way, yours too, until the way is clear.

The lesson passes as the Take-off lesson does, once you are in the air (@lesson-takeoff).
